# Authoring a bundle

The canonical guide is
[`docs/authoring.md`](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/blob/main/docs/authoring.md)
in the repository. This page exists so the docs lane can find it without
duplicating that text. Worked examples:

- [minimal](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/tree/main/docs/examples/minimal)
- [software-archive](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/tree/main/docs/examples/software-archive)
- [engineering-handbook](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/tree/main/docs/examples/engineering-handbook)
- [operations](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/tree/main/docs/examples/operations)
- [data-catalog](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/tree/main/docs/examples/data-catalog)

Check each example with the profile named in
[`docs/examples/README.md`](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/blob/main/docs/examples/README.md).
Current reader limits:
[`docs/compatibility.md`](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/blob/main/docs/compatibility.md).

`okmate init [path]` is create-only. Default path `knowledge`; default
scaffold is six type-first collections; `--bare` is index and log only.
Pass `docs`, `.okf`, or another directory when that is the bundle root.
See the [CLI](/docs/cli/) page and the repository README.
